# Blog SEO Rules — Somanath Studio

When creating or editing posts under `content/blog/**/*.mdx`, follow this checklist. Keep the honest engineering voice. Do not write polished agency fluff.

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
title: "Expressive H1-style title (can be longer)"
metaTitle: "SERP title ≤60 chars with primary keyword"
description: "120–160 chars. Include primary keyword + clear outcome. No fluff."
primaryKeyword: "main search phrase"
date: "YYYY-MM-DD"
updated: "YYYY-MM-DD"   # set whenever content meaningfully changes
readTime: "X min read"
category: "One of: SaaS MVP | Production Readiness | Next.js Performance | AI SaaS | Security | SaaS Architecture | Case Study | How We Work"
tags: ["3-6 specific tags"]
shareImage: "/images/blog/descriptive-kebab-name.png"  # 1200×630 preferred
relatedService: "/services/..."   # one commercial URL this post supports
intro: "Optional 1-sentence hook shown under H1"
faq:                              # optional; only if answers appear in the article
  - question: "..."
    answer: "..."
---
```

### Length rules
- `metaTitle`: **50–60 characters** (hard max 60). Do not append “— Somanath Studio” inside `metaTitle` (layout may add brand elsewhere).
- `description`: **120–160 characters**.
- Body: prefer **1,200+ words** for commercial/evergreen posts; news/security briefs can be shorter if dense and linked.

## Structure

1. One H1 only — comes from `title` in the page template. **Do not add `#` H1 in MDX.**
2. Start with a hero image that has a descriptive alt:
   - Markdown: `![Concrete alt describing the visual + topic](/images/blog/....png)`
   - Or Next `Image` with non-empty `alt=`.
3. Open with 2–4 sentences stating who it’s for and the outcome.
4. Use `##` H2 sections (at least 4 for long posts). Use `###` for sub-points.
5. Include a practical checklist, table, or decision framework — not only opinion.
6. End with **Related Reading** (3–4 internal blog links) and a **Next step** CTA to `/contact` or the `relatedService` URL.

## Internal linking (required)

Every post must include:
- **≥2 links** to related `/blog/...` posts
- **≥1 link** to a commercial page (`relatedService`, `/contact`, `/hire-saas-mvp-developer`, or `/case-studies/...`)
- Natural anchor text (not “click here”)

Blog → Service → Contact funnel is preferred for commercial topics.

## Images & alt text

- Every image needs a unique, specific alt (what is shown + topic).
- Bad: `image`, `screenshot`, `diagram`
- Good: `Next.js App Router caching flow for a multi-tenant SaaS dashboard`
- Prefer WebP/PNG under `/public/images/blog/`
- Set `shareImage` in frontmatter (don’t rely on generic `/og` fallback)

## Schema (handled by `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`)

The site auto-emits:
- `BlogPosting` (headline, dates, author, publisher, image, keywords, wordCount, breadcrumbs)
- Optional `FAQPage` when `faq:` is present in frontmatter

You do **not** paste raw JSON-LD into MDX. Keep `faq` answers consistent with visible on-page FAQ content.

## Keyword usage

- Put `primaryKeyword` in: `metaTitle`, first 100 words, one H2, and naturally 2–4 times in body.
- Do not stuff keywords. Prefer clear founder/engineer language.
- Secondary phrases go in H2s and tags.

## Voice & compliance

- Honest, technical, founder-facing.
- Label metrics clearly (verified client result vs illustrative).
- No fake testimonials, no invented stats.
- Prefer “senior-led / flexible team” commercial framing over “I alone do everything” when discussing delivery.

## Copy-paste prompt for new posts

Use this prompt when drafting a new article:

```text
Write a new SomSite blog post as MDX for content/blog/<slug>.mdx.

Topic: <TOPIC>
Primary keyword: <KEYWORD>
Related service URL: <SERVICE_PATH>
Audience: SaaS founders / technical buyers
Goal: rank + convert to /contact or the related service

Requirements:
1. Frontmatter with title, metaTitle (≤60 chars), description (120–160), primaryKeyword, date, updated, readTime, category, tags (3–6), shareImage path, relatedService, optional faq (2–4 Q&As that also appear in the article).
2. No H1 in the body. Use ## / ### only.
3. 1,200+ words unless this is a short security/news brief.
4. Hero image markdown with descriptive alt text.
5. Practical sections: problem, what breaks, how to evaluate, checklist, when to get help.
6. ≥2 internal blog links and ≥1 link to relatedService or /contact.
7. Related Reading + Next step CTA.
8. Honest engineering tone. No agency fluff. No keyword stuffing.
9. If citing performance/cost numbers, label them as verified, internal, or illustrative.
```

## Before finishing an edit

- [ ] metaTitle ≤60
- [ ] description 120–160
- [ ] primaryKeyword + relatedService set
- [ ] shareImage set (or note why fallback is OK)
- [ ] all images have alt
- [ ] no MDX `#` H1
- [ ] ≥2 blog links + ≥1 commercial link
- [ ] updated date bumped on material changes
